WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:04.886
Hello, everyone! I'm Mr. Jake. Welcome to Online A two, Book two.

2
00:00:05.186 --> 00:00:08.700
Hi! I'm Sreypich. Let's learn together!

3
00:00:09.000 --> 00:00:15.100
Unit seventeen: Endangered Animals. In this unit, you will talk about results with the first conditional.

4
00:00:16.117 --> 00:00:17.129
Endangered.

5
00:00:17.829 --> 00:00:21.025
Endangered means in danger of disappearing forever.

6
00:00:21.325 --> 00:00:23.289
The Mekong dolphin is endangered.

7
00:00:23.989 --> 00:00:26.572
Your turn. Say: Endangered.

8
00:00:29.272 --> 00:00:30.285
Endangered.

9
00:00:31.283 --> 00:00:32.157
Species.

10
00:00:32.857 --> 00:00:35.228
Species means a group of similar animals.

11
00:00:35.528 --> 00:00:37.969
This species lives only in Cambodia.

12
00:00:38.669 --> 00:00:41.541
Your turn. Say: Species.

13
00:00:44.241 --> 00:00:45.196
Species.

14
00:00:46.183 --> 00:00:47.208
Habitat.

15
00:00:47.908 --> 00:00:50.186
Habitat means the natural home of an animal.

16
00:00:50.486 --> 00:00:52.950
Farms are replacing the elephants' habitat.

17
00:00:53.650 --> 00:00:56.767
Your turn. Say: Habitat.

18
00:00:59.467 --> 00:01:00.433
Habitat.

19
00:01:01.417 --> 00:01:02.197
Protect.

20
00:01:02.897 --> 00:01:05.013
Protect means to keep safe from harm.

21
00:01:05.313 --> 00:01:07.150
Rangers protect the animals.

22
00:01:07.850 --> 00:01:10.177
Your turn. Say: Protect.

23
00:01:12.877 --> 00:01:13.739
Protect.

24
00:01:14.750 --> 00:01:15.391
Hunt.

25
00:01:16.091 --> 00:01:18.358
Hunt means to chase and kill animals.

26
00:01:18.658 --> 00:01:20.553
It is illegal to hunt tigers.

27
00:01:21.253 --> 00:01:23.998
Your turn. Say: Hunt.

28
00:01:26.698 --> 00:01:27.455
Hunt.

29
00:01:28.450 --> 00:01:29.277
Tiger.

30
00:01:29.977 --> 00:01:32.929
Tiger means a big orange cat with black stripes.

31
00:01:33.229 --> 00:01:34.938
Tigers are very rare now.

32
00:01:35.638 --> 00:01:38.162
Your turn. Say: Tiger.

33
00:01:40.862 --> 00:01:41.678
Tiger.

34
00:01:42.683 --> 00:01:43.568
Elephant.

35
00:01:44.268 --> 00:01:47.162
Elephant means a very large grey animal with a trunk.

36
00:01:47.462 --> 00:01:49.519
Wild elephants live in Mondulkiri.

37
00:01:50.219 --> 00:01:52.895
Your turn. Say: Elephant.

38
00:01:55.595 --> 00:01:56.422
Elephant.

39
00:01:57.417 --> 00:01:58.336
Save.

40
00:01:59.036 --> 00:02:01.268
Save means to keep from danger or death.

41
00:02:01.568 --> 00:02:03.417
We can save endangered animals.

42
00:02:04.117 --> 00:02:06.955
Your turn. Say: Save.

43
00:02:09.655 --> 00:02:10.389
Save.

44
00:02:11.383 --> 00:02:13.383
Now let's listen to a conversation.

45
00:02:13.683 --> 00:02:17.099
Sreypich, why are some animals endangered?

46
00:02:18.383 --> 00:02:20.650
People destroy their habitat and hunt them.

47
00:02:21.950 --> 00:02:23.659
What will happen if we do nothing?

48
00:02:24.950 --> 00:02:27.309
If we do nothing, tigers will disappear.

49
00:02:28.617 --> 00:02:29.966
And if we protect them?

50
00:02:31.250 --> 00:02:34.434
If we protect habitats, animals will survive.

51
00:02:35.750 --> 00:02:39.514
Grammar focus: If plus present, will plus verb.

52
00:02:39.814 --> 00:02:42.557
If we protect habitats, animals will survive.

53
00:02:42.857 --> 00:02:47.144
Use the present simple after 'if' (not 'will'): If we protect them ...

54
00:02:48.150 --> 00:02:51.011
Now read and listen. Saving Our Wildlife.

55
00:02:51.311 --> 00:02:53.009
Some animals are endangered.

56
00:02:54.317 --> 00:02:58.650
When people destroy their habitat or hunt them, fewer animals survive.

57
00:02:59.950 --> 00:03:03.424
Many people work hard to protect and save tigers and elephants.

58
00:03:04.717 --> 00:03:08.017
If we protect forests, these species will survive.

59
00:03:09.317 --> 00:03:11.781
If we do nothing, our children will never see them.

60
00:03:13.083 --> 00:03:15.654
Quiz time! Choose the correct answer.

61
00:03:15.954 --> 00:03:18.976
If we protect habitats, animals blank survive.

62
00:03:19.276 --> 00:03:21.942
A, will. B, would. C, are.

63
00:03:25.950 --> 00:03:27.624
The answer is A: will.

64
00:03:29.117 --> 00:03:31.615
If people blank tigers, they will disappear.

65
00:03:31.915 --> 00:03:35.209
A, hunt. B, will hunt. C, hunted.

66
00:03:39.217 --> 00:03:40.647
The answer is A: hunt.

67
00:03:42.150 --> 00:03:44.568
In danger of disappearing forever means blank.

68
00:03:44.868 --> 00:03:48.405
A, endangered. B, protected. C, wild.

69
00:03:52.417 --> 00:03:54.416
The answer is A: endangered.

70
00:03:55.917 --> 00:03:59.916
Now it's your turn to speak. What can we do to save endangered animals?

71
00:04:05.216 --> 00:04:12.059
If we stop cutting down forests, elephants will keep their homes. If we tell people about the problem, more people will help.

72
00:04:12.359 --> 00:04:14.196
Excellent answer, Sreypich!

73
00:04:15.183 --> 00:04:19.902
Great work today! You learned eight new words and if plus present, will plus verb.

74
00:04:20.202 --> 00:04:24.178
Today's value is protecting wildlife. Protect animals and their homes.

75
00:04:24.478 --> 00:04:27.003
See you in Unit eighteen. Goodbye!

76
00:04:27.303 --> 00:04:30.559
Thank you, Mr. Jake! Bye, everyone!

